Z||000000||trigger||04-12-2001||07:42 PM||||There are some wires down by the fuse block on my 88 coupe automatic, and I am not sure what they are for.  They look like factory wiring.  Both wires have female, plastic connectors with clips.  The colors are as follows: orange, always hot, grey connector; pink, hot when ignition is on, blue connector.  Both wires come down out of the dash, side by side.  Thanks for any info.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||04-12-2001||11:19 PM||||Orange, hot when door is open-for lower lighting package or power trunk release if hot with door closed.<BR>Blue, cruise control?||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||04-12-2001||11:31 PM||||What power options do you have in your car?  Locks, windows, mirrors?<P>way up in the furthest corner of the dash there is a little junction box.  I remember those colors being there, and being the +12v feeds for the power locks and windows.<P>You may be able to see it way up there, it is white in color and just snaps into the frame of the car.  There will also be another orange and white wire up there, those are the feeds for the overhead courtesy lights.<P>If you dont have any of these options, you dont need to really worry about them.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||trigger||04-12-2001||11:51 PM||||I have a power trunk release, cruise, and all of the courtesy lights.   it's not actually a blue wire but a blue connector on a pink wire.<BR>FieroJoe, would my 88 be factory wired for power windows then?  I know it would be a lot easier for me.  Otherwise, I'm going to try talking my mechanic out of the power windows on one of his 84 SE parts cars.<P>Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
